From d3e915f4ed534be8cddebc38b5dbe882a7cccf57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fx-fork <fx-fork@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:15:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] IV-0002 Add OpenCode Zen and OpenCode Go providers

Route opencode/<model> to https://opencode.ai/zen/v1 and
opencode-go/<model> to https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1 over an
OpenAI Chat Completions transport with streamed tool calls,
reasoning deltas, usage, and keep-alive tolerant SSE parsing.

One credential source covers both fleets: OPENCODE_API_KEY or a
stored key in ~/.fx/opencode-auth.json saved by 'fx login
opencode|opencode-go'. Model namespaces disambiguate identical
model ids across OpenCode, the Codex subscription, and the AI
Gateway; mismatched model/credential pairs fail with actionable
errors, and selecting an OpenCode model adopts its credential
when it resolves.

Capabilities advertise tool use with conservative family context
windows. Focused tests run via 'zig build test-opencode'.
